{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:08cf853e451c4fa4","name":"Droid Commander","source":{"id":"source:reference-08cf853e451c4fa4","title":"Droid Commander","revision":19880,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:47:06Z","sha256":"c87ebb2a2a47607be73ccc4f561f5c40874594c7c82a383c349b1669f960f748","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19880","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Droid%20Commander&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-08cf853e451c4fa4","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["All armies need an established hierarchy to ensure that objectives are achieved successfully. Even Battle Droids, with their network connection to a central command computer, must sometimes have specific movements dictated to them by a separate ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," designated as a field commander. The Droid Commander, through the course of its career as a soldier for its organization, proves itself through its actions and is promoted to lead others of its kind to support the unit's mission and the organization's cause.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Droid Commanders are easy to spot on the battlefield. They bear command colors and are positioned within the ranks to receive maximum protection from the enemy. Although they might be easy to find, they are rarely easy to eliminate. Because these ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," are prized by their superiors, they are augmented and improved to increase the likelihood of their survival and continued service to their masters. Better weapons, armor and equipment in addition to upgraded systems make the Droid Commander a formidable foe on its own. Its ability to effectively lead troops on the battlefield make the Droid Commander and its squad a force to be reckoned with.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Examples of Droid Commanders in Star Wars:"]}," OLR-4, OOM-9, OOM-14.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Prerequisites:"]}," To qualify to become a Droid Commander, a character must fulfill the following criteria:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Minimum Level:"]}," 7th"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Trained Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained_Skills"},":"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Tactics)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Tactics)"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"},":"]}," Any one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talent"}," from either the\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Leadership Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Leadership_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:a51a0918ead13923"}," or"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Commando Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commando_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:1ccfc7af27121192"}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," Must be a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}]}]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Game Rule Information"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Droid Commanders have the following game statistics:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",